# The file questions, asked by their own keys and answered by the script.
#
# Every open and save goes through one picker. The app's is the Windows dialog (or
# BertBrowser); a scripted run's answers from pose-pick, so the code on both sides of the
# question is the app's own and nothing appears on the desktop.

sample clip.mp4 6
sample more.mp4 4

# Unposed, the keys that ask are still refused: nothing here may open a dialog by accident.
# The toolbar's front door on an empty editor reads as opening, not appending.
pose-pick clip.mp4
intent AppendSource
assert-picked open Open a video
assert-has-media
assert-segments 1

# With something open it is an append, and it starts beside what is already there.
pose-pick more.mp4
key Ctrl+A
assert-picked open Add a video
assert-segments 2

# Backing out of the question changes nothing.
pose-pick cancel
key Ctrl+A
assert-segments 2

pose-pick cancel
key Ctrl+E
assert-picked save Save as
assert-segments 2

# Ctrl+O replaces what is open.
pose-pick more.mp4
key Ctrl+O
assert-picked open Open a video
assert-segments 1
shot 01-picked
